  "knownLimits": [
    "The whole composition moves, including the gentle background gradient. Rows 0-15 repeat the original top row, so that band (about 13 px in the native master) has no vertical gradient. Compared with the original rows 0-15 it differs by a mean of 0.6, a 99th percentile of 2 and a maximum of 9 RGB levels. The band was not perceptible in the inspected boards.",
    "Horizontal placement is unchanged: the source sun and disc bounds stay 0.5 px left of center at 1254 px, as approved.",
    "Integer threshold bounds can only report half-pixel centers. After resampling, the 216 px sun bounds read 0.5 px high and the 144 px sun bounds read 0.5 px left, while the disc bounds are exactly centered vertically at every size.",
    "Coverage centroids remain up to 0.35 px high at 1024 px and 0.12 px at 216 px. The approved rays differ slightly in area (13575-13826 px), so the source mask centroid already sits 0.37 px high at 1254 px with exact bounds. This is glyph asymmetry, not placement.",
    "Browser grayscale represents the disabled state but does not prove native SwiftUI saturation(0) pixels.",
